# Provenance drift: the 30-hash manifest vs the pinned originals

Date: 2026-09-30 (America/Toronto). Read-only with respect to every repository,
worktree, the manifest, and all pinned files. All writes were to this output
directory. Raw evidence in `evidence/`; full per-file table in `DRIFT.tsv`.

**Headline.** The 13/30 mismatch is **reproduced by my own recomputation** (not taken
from the feasibility report). **All 13 drifted files are generated artifacts, not
hand-written inputs.** The manifest pinned the *outputs of preparation attempt-01*
(2026-09-28); a later run of the same prep tool (attempt-03, 2026-09-29 13:26 local)
**regenerated the same output paths in place against a different candidate worktree**.
The pinned content is fully recoverable and hash-verified inside the attempt-01
attempt directory. The defect is the prep step's shared output path, not tampering
with hand-written inputs. Recommended remedy: **do not re-pin**; restore the
`architecture-candidate-inputs` tree verbatim from attempt-01's retained outputs and
fix the prep step to write per-attempt output dirs. Details and limits below.

