## 3. Ruling on the 11 hxml files: GENERATED ARTIFACTS (evidence-backed)

Three independent lines of evidence:

1. **Content is machine-expanded.** Each file is an expansion of a hand-written
   driver `engine-haxe/targets/<target>.hxml` (via its include chain
   `targets/<t>.hxml → kotlin-common/common/classes.hxml`) with a mechanical prefix
   replacement `.haxelib/boring/git` → an absolute candidate-worktree path, plus a
   leading `-v`. The self-describing diff is retained per file in
   `out/architecture-candidate-inputs/diffs/<t>.hxml.diff`
   (header: `--- expanded-source(engine-haxe/targets/dart.hxml)` /
   `+++ out/architecture-candidate-inputs/hxml/dart.hxml`).
2. **The generator self-identifies.** The sibling `mapping-manifest.json` (same
   mtime 13:26) records `attempt: attempt-03-20260929T172659Z-2627546`,
   `toolRevision: 2`, per-bundle `prefixReplacements`, `noOldPrefixRemaining`,
   `leadingV` checks — i.e. a deterministic generation step, generator
   `out/architecture-t2/prepare.py` (present on disk).
3. **The pinned content is attempt-01's output, byte for byte.** I hashed every file
   under `out/architecture-t2/attempt-01-20260928T093930Z-1613971/outputs/` and
   matched **all 15** manifest `originals` hashes against attempt-01's retained
   outputs (13 changed files plus the 2 unchanged ones), including all 3 candidate
   JSONs (evidence/recompute-full.txt companion run; method above, output in
   `evidence/attempt-01-manifest.json` context). Attempt-01's hxml reference
   `/home/losses/Development/tq-workspace/boring-wt-architecture/...`; attempt-03's
   regenerated files reference
   `/home/losses/Development/tq-workspace/boring-wt-rust-candidate/...`
   (candidate HEAD `e1c65975…` per mapping-manifest.json).

**Consequence:** the drift is not an uncontrolled in-place write of hand-written
inputs. It is the prep tool's **attempt-03 run overwriting the shared output
directory `out/architecture-candidate-inputs/` that attempt-01 had written and that
the manifest had then pinned**. The hand-written sources
(`engine-haxe/targets/*.hxml`, consumer commit `8504d230`) were never touched; they
are not themselves hash-pinned by this manifest — that is a manifest design gap.

**Git history:** not available for these paths — `git status`/`git log` in the
consumer worktree show nothing for `out/architecture-candidate-inputs` (the whole
`out/` tree is untracked/gitignored). Blocker noted in §7; the attempt dirs are the
de-facto history and are sufficient.

