## 5. Runbook invariant assessment (quoted, not paraphrased)

`boring-wt-architecture/docs/investigations/architecture-round-2/p09-fixed-matrix-preparation-runbook.md`, §"Invariant re-verification after the run" (L249–256):

> After the matrix completes (or aborts), re-run and record: the 30-manifest
> hash recomputation; the 1366-entry compiler inventory digest; …
> **Any drift voids the attempt** and requires a new attempt dir; the drifted
> attempt is retained as historical evidence, never deleted or rewritten.

Precisely: the invariant recomputes the same 30 paths pinned in
`tiqian-fixed-2159c657-prep/manifest.json` and requires all 30 to equal their pinned
values. It is evaluated over **all 30, originals included**, not only the live
derived inputs. **The 13 mismatches trip it** — in fact it already fails *before*
the run: any P09 matrix run executed today would be voided at the post-run check,
and honestly also at any pre-run check, by drift that the stage commands themselves
did not cause (the stage commands consume the derived inputs; the runbook classifies
`out/architecture-candidate-inputs/` as "retained for provenance, **never a live
input**", L265).

## 6. Remedy (justified) — restore + fix the generator; do NOT re-pin

**Why not re-pin:** re-pinning would write attempt-03's hashes into a manifest whose
entire purpose is the `fixed-2159c657` preparation — but attempt-03's outputs are
the expansion against candidate `e1c65975`/`boring-wt-rust-candidate`, i.e. content
of a **different candidate lineage** than the manifest's derived inputs
(`publication-staging/fixed-compiler-2159c657/...`). Re-pinning would make the
check pass while pinning provably wrong-lineage provenance, and would legitimize
the in-place overwrite of already-pinned outputs. That is exactly the defect.

**Recommended, in order:**

1. **Restore the pinned originals byte-for-byte** from the retained attempt
   directory (all 15 verified as exact hash matches):
   `cp out/architecture-t2/attempt-01-20260929…/outputs/out/architecture-candidate-inputs/hxml/*.hxml out/architecture-candidate-inputs/hxml/` and the two JSONs from
   `…/outputs/`. After restore, re-run the 30-hash recomputation: expected 30/30
   match. (Not executed by me — pinned files are outside my write scope; the
   commands above are the proposal. No `REPIN.diff` is produced because re-pinning
   is explicitly not recommended.)
2. **Fix the prep step (the actual defect):** `out/architecture-t2/prepare.py`
   (toolRevision 2) must write to a per-attempt output directory
   (`out/architecture-t2/attempt-NN…/outputs/…`, which it already populates) and
   **never** also publish to the shared, manifest-pinned
   `out/architecture-candidate-inputs/` path. If a stable-path view is needed, make
   it a symlink-free copy made *before* the manifest is written and never rewritten.
3. **Record the deviation** (attempt-03's in-place rewrite) in the prep history:
   the drifted 13:26 state is preserved verbatim in
   `attempt-03-…/outputs/` and `mapping-manifest.json` — nothing is lost; a one-line
   note in the prep records (or a follow-up runbook amendment, per the feasibility
   report's staleness list) is enough.
4. **Optionally, in a future manifest revision**, pin the true hand-written sources
   (`engine-haxe/targets/*.hxml` at consumer `8504d230`) as originals, so provenance
   anchors sources rather than one generator's outputs.

